course: dictionary
lesson: 727
title: Words for rocks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Basalt is a noun, the name of a hard, dark rock. It forms when hot lava from a volcano cools quickly. «Basalt is a dark, fine-grained igneous rock made from runny lava and is the most common rock of the ocean floor.» The clues dark and runny lava tell you what basalt looks like and where it comes from.
explain: Basalt can also be used as an adjective, to describe something made of this rock, like basalt columns. Look at the words around it: the word after basalt names the thing, and basalt tells you what it is made of. Ask yourself, what kind of columns? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: In science lessons, basalt is a classic igneous rock, one that forms from cooled melted rock. When you meet a new rock name, look for the clues in the sentence first. Then, if you are still unsure, a dictionary or a science book will tell you more.
fact: Basalt is a hard, dark grey or black rock.
fact: Basalt forms when hot lava from a volcano cools quickly.
fact: Much of the ocean floor is made of basalt.
fact: The Giant's Causeway in Northern Ireland has basalt columns with six sides.
fact: Basalt is a classic igneous rock, so it is a useful example in rock lessons.
exercise: «Basalt is a dark, fine-grained igneous rock made from runny lava.» What is basalt? | A type of liquid that flows from volcanoes | *A hard, dark rock made when hot lava cools quickly | A small animal that lives under rocks | A soft, white rock found on beaches
exercise: «The walkers stared at the basalt columns of the Giant's Causeway.» What does basalt tell you about the columns? | *They are made of hard, dark rock | They are made of soft wood | They are made of water | They are very tall trees
exercise: «Basalt is the most common rock of the ocean floor.» Find and copy the word that names a kind of rock. | floor | *basalt | common | ocean
test: Basalt forms when what cools quickly? | Sand from a beach | Wood from old trees | Cold snow that melts in spring | *Hot lava from a volcano
test: «The lava cooled quickly, and the dark rock that formed was basalt.» What colour is basalt? | Bright green | Pure white | *Dark grey or black | Bright red
exam: Which famous place in Northern Ireland has six-sided basalt columns? | Blackpool Tower | The Sahara Desert | *The Giant's Causeway | Big Ben in London
